# The build context for Dockerfile, whose context is this repository
# root (it builds konturctl out of third_party/kontur and reads the
# commit stamp out of .git, neither of which is under the Go tree).
# Nothing else in this repo builds from here: packer/kontur's two builds
# each cd into their own directory first, and Dockerfile.build -- the
# toolchain image, which COPYs nothing -- carries its own
# Dockerfile.build.dockerignore excluding everything, which BuildKit
# prefers over this file for that build.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded: `go build` stamps bin/grain with the
# commit it came from and can only read that here.

# Build outputs and caches, none of which the image build reads and all
# of which are large: bin/grain is ~200 MB on its own, and shipping a
# host's node_modules would both bloat the context and risk `npm ci`
# resolving against a tree built for a different platform.
bin/
.container-cache/
ui/node_modules/
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
